1.text:
With the zero-sum order sheet

\begin{equation*}
b_{1}=+200,\;b_{2}=+100,\;b_{3}=-100,\;b_{4}=-200,\qquad
\sum b_{i}=0 ,
\end{equation*}
$B_{A}=b_{p_{A1}}+b_{p_{A2}}$ and $B_{W}+B_{L}=0$ put, calls being
ignored,

\begin{equation*}
X=C_{W}+100+B_{W},\qquad Y=C_{L}+B_{L},\qquad C_{W}+C_{L}=P ,
\end{equation*}
the $+100$ being the hand win.  The hand is won by the team which
contains $p_{1}$, $\max p_{W}<\max p_{L}$.  The hypothesis
$W\ne\{p_{1},p_{2}\}$ is $1\in W,\;2\notin W$.  Up to renaming

\begin{equation*}
W=\{p_{1},p_{3}\},L=\{p_{2},p_{4}\}\quad{\rm or}\quad 
W=\{p_{1},p_{4}\},L=\{p_{2},p_{3}\},
\end{equation*}
the first being the best for the eventual winner.  On the $1\!-\!3$
vs $2\!-\!4$ disposition

\begin{equation*}
B_{W}^{\max}=b_{1}+b_{3}=200-100=+100,\qquad 
B_{L}=b_{2}+b_{4}=100-200=-100,
\end{equation*}
and

\begin{equation*}
B_{W}-B_{L}=200~{\rm pt}
\end{equation*}
is the maximal order swing compatible with $W\ne\{p_{1},p_{2}\}$.
The first two tricks can be made point free and in the idealised
limit the whole point pool can be left in $p_{4}\in L$,

\begin{equation*}
C_{W}^{\max}=P,\qquad C_{L}^{\min}=0,\qquad C_{W}-C_{L}=P,
\end{equation*}
the familiar $P\approx100$ pt pure card advantage, $96$ pt on the
Mahjong $+1$, Dragon $-5$ normalisation $P_{0}$.  Hence on the ordinary
$+/-$ sheet, calls ignored,

\begin{equation*}
X_{\max}=P+100+B_{W}^{\max}=P+200,\qquad 
Y_{\min}=C_{L}^{\min}+B_{L}=-100,
\end{equation*}
and in net terms

\begin{equation*}
X-Y=(C_{W}-C_{L})+100+(B_{W}-B_{L})=P+100+200=P+300
\end{equation*}
net points won in the hand, $P$ pt of cards, $100$ pt for the hand
win and $200$ pt of order swing $1+3$ v $2+4$.

With the conventional book keeping $P=4\cdot5+4\cdot10+4K=100$

\begin{equation*}
X_{\max}=300,\qquad Y_{\min}=-100,\qquad 
X_{\max}-Y_{\min}=400~{\rm pt\;won},
\end{equation*}
i.e. $300$ pt credited to the winner and $-100$ pt credited to the
loser on the usual $+/-$ sheet.  On the exact Mahjong/Dragon
normalisation $P_{0}=96$,

\begin{equation*}
X_{\max}=P_{0}+200=296,\qquad Y_{\min}=-100,\qquad
X_{\max}-Y_{\min}=P_{0}+300=396,
\end{equation*}
$96$ pt cards $+100$ pt hand win $+200$ pt order swing, $196$ pt
card+win on the sheet.  Stripped of the zero-sum order bonuses the
textbook card+hand bound is $X_{0}=C_{W}+100$, $Y_{0}=C_{L}$,
$X_{0}-Y_{0}\le P+100$, $X_{0}^{\max}=P+100\approx200$, $196$ pt on
$P_{0}$, the $P+100$ bound being vacuous with respect to
$W\ne\{p_{1},p_{2}\}$.

This $P+300$ net, $P+200$ gross to the winner, is the call-free core.
A successful Tichu $+100/-100$ and a successful Grand Tichu
$+200/-200$ are superimposable on the core and are the source of the
usual call-inclusive $P+700\simeq800$, $796$ on $P_{0}$, figures. ∎

